{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789479208,"nonce":"dqjt8zxvIGe6Oza46ZMy4Vf1f2E=","title":"clippy on zyntax_embed tests fails on the plugin macro's feature gate","message":"`zrtl_plugin!` expands `#[cfg(feature = \"linked-into-host\")]` into the crate that invokes it. `crates/zyntax_embed/tests/static_plugin_registration.rs` invokes it and `zyntax_embed` declares no such feature, so `unexpected_cfgs` fires three times and `cargo clippy -p zyntax_embed --all-targets -- -D warnings` fails before it checks anything else.\n\nFix: declare the value in the workspace lints table (`check-cfg = ['cfg(feature, values(\"linked-into-host\"))']`), which every crate with `[lints] workspace = true` inherits, so any crate that expands the macro accepts the gate.","files":null}]}